module

public import StacksFrontier.Deformation.Examples.Linear.NodalCubicLocalLift

/-!
# The quotient condition of the Stacks 0DZ2 counterexample: `J'·Q' = z·Q'`

Ninth layer of the instantiation of `Deformation.FlatModuleLiftBaseChangeStatement`. Stacks 0DZ2
asks for an ideal `J' ⊆ P'` with `P'/J' = Q'/J'Q'`. For the counterexample `J' = Y·P'`, and the
content of that condition is the identity proved here:

**`J'·Q' = z·Q'`.**

In `Q₁` the defining relation gives `Y = z·(z + 1)` (`qRelationMul`, layer three), and `z + 1` is
a unit in `Q' = (Q₁)_{z+1}` by construction (`isUnit_zQ_add_one`). So the ideal generated by `Y`
in `Q'` is the ideal generated by `z` — the unit factor drops out. This is the whole reason the
quotient condition is local to `P'` and needs no transport from the base `NC`, which is the
design trade recorded in
`StacksFrontier.Deformation.Examples.Linear.NodalCubicQColumn`.

## What remained for `hquot`, and where it is

`hquot` is bijectivity of `Ideal.quotientMap (J'.map (algebraMap P' Q')) (algebraMap P' Q') _`,
i.e. of `P'/J' → Q'/J'Q'`. With the identity above, that map is `P'/(Y) → Q'/(z)`, and what is
left is the chain

`Q'/(z) ≅ Q₁/(z) ≅ P'/(Y)`,

whose two steps are: inverting `z + 1` does nothing modulo `z`, because `z + 1 ↦ 1` there; and
`Q₁/(z) = P'/(Y)` because `Q₁ = P'[z]/(z² + z − Y)` is `AdjoinRoot` and killing the root
substitutes `z = 0` into the relation, leaving `Y`. The surjection for the second step is already
available in the subring setting as
`Deformation.Examples.ArtinSchreier.quotByRoot`, with `quotByRoot_root` and
`quotByRoot_comp_algebraMap`; the same map over `P'` is `qOneToQuotOmega` (layer ten), its
injectivity is `ker_qOneToQuotOmega` (layer eleven), and the localization step together with
`hquot` itself is `bijective_quotientMap_omegaP` (layer twelve).

## Main results

* `Deformation.Examples.ArtinSchreier.isUnit_zQ_add_one`: `z + 1` is a unit in `Q'`.
* `Deformation.Examples.ArtinSchreier.algebraMap_omegaP_QBase`: `Y = z·(z + 1)` in `Q'`.
* `Deformation.Examples.ArtinSchreier.map_span_omegaP`: **`J'·Q' = z·Q'`**, the content of the
  quotient condition.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0DZ2](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0DZ2)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open Polynomial
open Deformation.Examples.MaurerCartanWindow

universe u

namespace Deformation.Examples.ArtinSchreier

/-- The image of the Artin–Schreier root `z` in `Q'`. -/
def zQ : QBase := algebraMap QOne QBase zRoot

/-- **`z + 1` is a unit in `Q'`**, by construction of `Q' = (Q₁)_{z+1}`. -/
theorem isUnit_zQ_add_one : IsUnit (algebraMap QOne QBase (zRoot + 1)) :=
  IsLocalization.map_units _
    (⟨zRoot + 1, Submonoid.mem_powers _⟩ : Submonoid.powers (zRoot + 1))

/-- **`Y = z·(z + 1)` in `Q'`**, the image of the relation `qRelationMul` of `Q₁`. -/
theorem algebraMap_omegaP_QBase :
    algebraMap PBase QBase omegaP = zQ * algebraMap QOne QBase (zRoot + 1) := by
  rw [IsScalarTower.algebraMap_apply PBase QOne QBase omegaP, qRelationMul, map_mul]
  rfl

/-- **The quotient condition's content: `J'·Q' = z·Q'`.** The ideal generated in `Q'` by
`Y = z·(z + 1)` is the ideal generated by `z`, because `z + 1` is a unit there. This is what makes
the quotient condition of Stacks 0DZ2 a statement inside `P'` rather than one transported from
the base. -/
theorem map_span_omegaP :
    (Ideal.span {omegaP}).map (algebraMap PBase QBase) = Ideal.span {zQ} := by
  rw [Ideal.map_span]
  have himg : (algebraMap PBase QBase) '' {omegaP} = {zQ * algebraMap QOne QBase (zRoot + 1)} := by
    rw [Set.image_singleton, algebraMap_omegaP_QBase]
  rw [himg]
  exact Ideal.span_singleton_mul_right_unit isUnit_zQ_add_one zQ

end Deformation.Examples.ArtinSchreier

end
